        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "гора (gorá) from Proto-Slavic gora — inherited, related to Sanskrit girí-, \"mountain\", Avestan gairi- and Lithuanian girià, \"forest\" (Vasmer). Bulgarian гора (gorá) still means \"forest\"."
            }
          ]
        },
